' ==========================================
' 18. Organization Invite Flow
' ==========================================
newpage Organization Invite Flow

actor "Admin/Owner" as AdminUser
participant "Client App" as App
participant "API Server" as API
participant "OrgContextMW" as OrgMW
participant "OrgService" as OrgSvc
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

note over AdminUser, DB
  Admins and Owners can invite new members
  to their organization via email.
  Plan-based limits enforced.
end note

== Send Invitation ==

AdminUser -> App: Click "Invite Member"
App -> API: POST /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/invitations\n[Authorization: Bearer <token>]\n{ "email": "new@example.com", "role": "VIEWER" }

API -> API: AuthMiddleware (verify token)
API -> OrgMW: RequireOrg(orgId)\nRequireOrgRole(ADMIN)

OrgMW -> DB: SELECT * FROM org_members\nWHERE org_id = ? AND user_id = ?
DB --> OrgMW: Membership record

alt Active ADMIN or OWNER
    OrgMW -> API: Continue

    API -> OrgSvc: InviteMember(orgId, email, role)

    OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT plan_tier FROM organizations\nWHERE id = ?
    DB --> OrgSvc: Organization (plan_tier)

    OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM org_members\nWHERE org_id = ?
    DB --> OrgSvc: Current member count

    OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM org_invitations\nWHERE org_id = ? AND status = 'PENDING'
    DB --> OrgSvc: Pending invitation count

    alt Total exceeds plan limit
        OrgSvc --> API: Error: plan limit reached
        API --> App: 403 Forbidden\n{ "error": "plan_limit_reached" }
    else Within limit
        OrgSvc -> OrgSvc: Generate unique token\n(32 random bytes hex)

        OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_invitations\n(org_id, email, role, token, status='PENDING',\nexpires_at = NOW() + 7 days)
        DB --> OrgSvc: Invitation record

        OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_audit_log\n(action='member.invited', metadata={email, role})
        DB --> OrgSvc: Audit entry

        OrgSvc --> API: Invitation
        API --> App: 201 Created\n{ "id": "uuid", "token": "abc...", "email": "..." }
    end

else Suspended or not a member
    OrgMW --> API: 403 Forbidden
    API --> App: 403 Forbidden\n{ "error": "insufficient_permissions" }
end

' ==========================================
' 19. Organization Accept Invitation Flow
' ==========================================
newpage Organization Accept Invitation Flow

actor "Invited User" as Invitee
participant "Client App" as App
participant "API Server" as API
participant "OrgService" as OrgSvc
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

note over Invitee, DB
  Any authenticated user can accept
  an invitation using the token.
  Creates org_member entry.
end note

== Accept Invitation ==

Invitee -> App: Click invitation link / enter token
App -> API: POST /api/v1/invitations/{token}/accept\n[Authorization: Bearer <token>]

API -> API: AuthMiddleware (verify user)
API -> OrgSvc: AcceptInvitation(token, userID)

OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT * FROM org_invitations\nWHERE token = ? AND status = 'PENDING'
DB --> OrgSvc: Invitation record

alt Invitation found
    OrgSvc -> OrgSvc: Check expiration\n(expires_at > NOW()?)

    alt Expired
        OrgSvc -> DB: UPDATE org_invitations\nSET status = 'EXPIRED'
        OrgSvc --> API: Error: invitation expired
        API --> App: 410 Gone\n{ "error": "invitation_expired" }
    else Valid
        OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT * FROM org_members\nWHERE org_id = ? AND user_id = ?
        DB --> OrgSvc: Check existing membership

        alt Already a member
            OrgSvc --> API: Error: already a member
            API --> App: 409 Conflict\n{ "error": "already_member" }
        else New member
            OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_members\n(org_id, user_id, role, status='ACTIVE',\ninvited_by)
            DB --> OrgSvc: Member record

            OrgSvc -> DB: UPDATE org_invitations\nSET status = 'ACCEPTED'
            DB --> OrgSvc: Success

            OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_audit_log\n(action='member.joined', metadata={role})
            DB --> OrgSvc: Audit entry

            OrgSvc --> API: Member
            API --> App: 200 OK\n{ "org_id": "...", "role": "VIEWER" }
        end
    end
else Invitation not found
    OrgSvc --> API: Error: not found
    API --> App: 404 Not Found
end

' ==========================================
' 20. Organization Suspend/Unsuspend Flow
' ==========================================
newpage Organization Suspend/Unsuspend Flow

actor "Admin/Owner" as AdminUser
participant "Client App" as App
participant "API Server" as API
participant "OrgContextMW" as OrgMW
participant "OrgService" as OrgSvc
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

note over AdminUser, DB
  Admins can suspend members (except OWNER).
  Suspended members cannot access org data
  but still count toward member limit.
end note

== Suspend Member ==

AdminUser -> App: Click "Suspend" on member
App -> API: PUT /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/members/{memberId}/suspend\n[Authorization: Bearer <token>]

API -> API: AuthMiddleware (verify token)
API -> OrgMW: RequireOrg + RequireOrgRole(ADMIN)

OrgMW -> DB: Verify actor is active ADMIN+
OrgMW --> API: Continue

API -> OrgSvc: SuspendMember(orgId, memberId, actorId)

OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT * FROM org_members\nWHERE id = ? AND org_id = ?
DB --> OrgSvc: Target member

alt Target is OWNER
    OrgSvc --> API: Error: cannot suspend owner
    API --> App: 403 Forbidden\n{ "error": "cannot_suspend_owner" }
else Target is not OWNER
    OrgSvc -> DB: UPDATE org_members\nSET status = 'SUSPENDED',\nsuspended_by = ?, suspended_at = NOW()
    DB --> OrgSvc: Success

    OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_audit_log\n(action='member.suspended', metadata={member_id})
    DB --> OrgSvc: Audit entry

    OrgSvc --> API: Success
    API --> App: 200 OK
end

== Unsuspend Member ==

AdminUser -> App: Click "Unsuspend" on member
App -> API: PUT /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/members/{memberId}/unsuspend\n[Authorization: Bearer <token>]

API -> OrgMW: RequireOrg + RequireOrgRole(ADMIN)
API -> OrgSvc: UnsuspendMember(orgId, memberId, actorId)

OrgSvc -> DB: SELECT * FROM org_members\nWHERE id = ? AND org_id = ?
DB --> OrgSvc: Target member

alt Status is SUSPENDED
    OrgSvc -> DB: UPDATE org_members\nSET status = 'ACTIVE',\nsuspended_by = NULL, suspended_at = NULL
    DB --> OrgSvc: Success

    OrgSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO org_audit_log\n(action='member.unsuspended')
    DB --> OrgSvc: Audit entry

    OrgSvc --> API: Success
    API --> App: 200 OK
else Not suspended
    OrgSvc --> API: Error: not suspended
    API --> App: 400 Bad Request
end

